body:
CI tests were failing because `apps/console/dev/__tests__/ObjectView.test.tsx` lacked mocks for dependencies that `ObjectView` requires to render. Without these mocks, the component failed to initialize, causing tests to error when querying DOM elements.

## Changes

Added mocks for:
- **Core hooks**: `@object-ui/permissions`, `@object-ui/i18n`, `@object-ui/collaboration`, `@object-ui/react`
- **UI notifications**: `sonner` toast API
- **Plugin components**: `@object-ui/plugin-detail`, `@object-ui/plugin-view`, `@object-ui/plugin-charts`
- **Action system**: `@object-ui/app-shell` `useObjectActions` hook

Example of added mock structure:

```typescript
vi.mock('@object-ui/permissions', () => ({
    usePermissions: () => ({ can: () => true }),
}));

vi.mock('@object-ui/app-shell', async (importOriginal) => {
    const actual = await importOriginal<any>();
    return {
        ...actual,
        useObjectActions: () => ({
            execute: vi.fn(),
            create: vi.fn(),
            deleteRecord: vi.fn(),
            loading: false,
            error: null,
        }),
    };
});
```

This resolves 18 test failures where elements like `view-tab-menu-config-all` were not found due to incomplete component rendering.
